  {
    "episode_id": 95850,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95850.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "Well, good morning, Rich. You know, it's really entirely up to the Democrats at this point. They control the House. They control the Senate and the White House. They're going to have to make some real tough decisions. And I can tell you that a lot of Americans across the country are very angry about the level of spending. And if they want to get serious about avoiding a government shutdown, they've got to make some tough choices and prioritize what they want in these upcoming packages. Because I can tell you for myself, for several of our colleagues, especially in North Florida, we will not stand by while they bankrupt this country.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The Democrats control the House.",
        "confidence": 0.98
      },
      {
        "text": "The Democrats control the Senate.",
        "confidence": 0.98
      },
      {
        "text": "The Democrats control the White House.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "It is up to the Democrats to make tough decisions regarding government funding.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "Many Americans are angry about current levels of government spending.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Avoiding a government shutdown requires making tough choices and prioritizing budgetary needs.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Some members of Congress from North Florida oppose policies that lead to national bankruptcy.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Government spending is currently unsustainable and risks economic collapse.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes that fiscal responsibility should take precedence over political expediency.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The audience values economic stability and views excessive debt negatively.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Political leaders have a moral obligation to prevent national financial ruin.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker has legitimate standing to speak on behalf of constituents in North Florida.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 95850,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95850.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "We've been working with your office to try to get a better idea in the weeks since the full pull out of troops out of Afghanistan, the number of Americans and especially Floridians who have safely been evacuated. I understand you have an update on that. And specifically, we're talking about 311 people from your congressional district.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "We have been working with your office to gain a clearer understanding of the evacuation situation following the complete withdrawal of U.S. troops from Afghanistan.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "The focus has been on identifying how many American citizens were safely evacuated after the troop withdrawal from Afghanistan.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "Special emphasis has been placed on determining the number of evacuees from Florida.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "I believe you currently have updated information regarding the evacuation numbers.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The specific group under discussion consists of 311 individuals from your congressional district.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The speaker trusts that the recipient’s office possesses accurate and timely data on the evacuation efforts.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The evacuation process was coordinated through official channels involving the speaker’s office and the recipient’s office.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "It is important to track and report evacuation figures by geographic region, particularly at the state and congressional district levels.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The recipient has access to reliable records of individual evacuee locations and affiliations.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "There is an expectation that the recipient will provide a formal update on the matter.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 95850,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95850.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, so we have about 300 plus of individuals that have ties to our district and the surrounding region that we have gotten out of Afghanistan. I couldn't be more proud of our team and the work that they have done over the last month in really navigating this very complex threat environment. And that is something we're very proud of, but there's still a lot of folks that got left behind and we still have Americans from our district that are in Afghanistan. And so we're going to continue to work on getting those folks out. In fact, last night we passed out of the House of Representatives a plan and a bill that includes funding to get our people home. because even though President Biden thinks that the mission is complete, we will not stop until every single American is boots on the ground here in America.",
