    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95850.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "Yes, every person that we are working with is desperate to come home. They have made several attempts. Many of the people that we had, we were able to get up to the gate at the airport in Kabul, and they were rejected. They were turned away, even though they had passports, even though they had all the papers in place, they were turned away. And when the military mission ended early, they were less stranded. And so we have been having to bounce them around from safe house to safe house and look for alternative routes to get them to a neighboring country where they can then be evacuated from that country.",
